{
 "about": "General quantity concepts (not specific to any product category). Each concept has a kind of quantity (its dimension), the terms by which it is named (anchors in language), and declared semantic properties. Selection rule (X1 section 6): a concept is included if it is a quantity kind of the metrology frame, or if its naming term recurs as a declaration label in at least two development categories (census of development records, 2026-10-21). Several concepts may share a term (polysemy, for example 'capacity' or 'size'); the dimension of the unit chooses among them, and a term never identifies a concept whose dimension disagrees with the unit. Authored by the developer; tier: definitions. X2: 'generic' marks the concept that an unnamed dimensioned value of that dimension denotes ('the magnitude of that dimension of the named thing'); new concepts from development labels and the metrology frame.",
 "provenance": {
  "source": "metrology frame + census of development-category labels",
  "holder": "developer",
  "basis": "definition"
 },
